      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 American College of Foot and Ankle Surgeons. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The use of cannulated instruments under fluoroscopy can improve the localization of the anteromedial and posterolateral portals for use in ankle arthroscopy. This technique is valuable for the less-experienced ankle arthroscopist, in resident education, and for the experienced arthroscopist when surface anatomy palpation and visualization is less than ideal due to soft tissue edema and obesity."
